<title>JAPAN: MOF says big Japan firms want 110-115 dlr/yen - Jiji.</title>
<headline>MOF says big Japan firms want 110-115 dlr/yen - Jiji.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Large Japanese firms believe an exchange rate of 110-115 yen to the dollar is reasonable, Eisuke Sakakibara, director-general of the Ministry of Finance's International Finance Bureau, was quoted as saying by Jiji news agency on Thursday.</p>
</text>
